{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_3",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "It is well known that electricity consumption is the dominant source of energy in the hotel industry and that energy use is the major source of carbon emissions in this sector [10, 17-19]. ... These contributors to energy use are related to physical building characteristics, and less or no attention was given to those contributors related to economic, environmental, or social outcomes.",
      "reason": "The Introduction describes the current state of knowledge (dominant energy sources, typical variables studied) and identifies the uncertainty/gap that economic, environmental, and social contributors have received little attention."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "The research fulfils the lack of systematic reviews and meta-analyses considering energy use and its contributors in hotel buildings and the lack of theoretical frameworks on these relationships.",
      "reason": "The Introduction explicitly explains the need and importance of conducting the review, including practical relevance for practitioners, academics, and legislators."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "A search for previous reviews was done, but neither a systematic review nor a meta-analysis involving energy use and its contributors in hotels was found until the day before the protocol registration, October 26, 2023.",
      "reason": "The authors report having searched for similar reviews and found none, thereby explaining the need for the current review; the Literature Review also distinguishes the review from related but non-overlapping meta-analyses."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "This is a review of observational relationships between contributors and energy use in hotel buildings, not a review of intervention effects, so no mechanism of action is required."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The review does not evaluate a complex intervention or delivery context; it synthesizes correlations between building/economic/social/environmental variables and energy use, so a logic model is not required."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 90
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_4",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "This systematic review and meta-analysis aim to identify contributors to energy use in hotel buildings, provide a descriptive picture of the research stream, and synthesize the theoretical foundation in each variable, and determine the magnitude of the mean effect size on hotels' energy use.",
      "reason": "The Introduction explicitly states the review's objectives: identify contributors, describe the research stream, synthesize theory, and estimate mean effect sizes. The abstract (text_2) and conclusion (text_15) reiterate the objective. However, no formal question-formulation framework (e.g., PICO, SPIDER) is named; the objectives are stated directly, which satisfies the explicit statement requirement."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e2",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "This review used meta-analysis on bivariate correlation coefficients, which are natural candidates to be an index of effect magnitude suitable for cumulation across studies",
      "reason": "This is a review of correlational associations between contributors and hotel energy use, not a review of intervention effects, so PICO-style planned comparisons do not apply."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 90
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_5",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "To be included, the studies must use quantitative data and investigate the relationship between at least one independent variable (floor area, occupancy rate, number of rooms, carbon intensity, water use, among others) and the energy use in hotel buildings. These variables were always related to hotels or hotel chains of all levels (star rating), open or closed companies. The included studies have assessed the relationships among the variables using univariate or multivariate statistics techniques (i.e., correlations and/or regressions).",
      "reason": "Study design (quantitative correlational/regression studies), setting (hotel buildings/chains of all star ratings), and required variables are explicitly specified as eligibility criteria."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "In the report characteristics, there were no restrictions about the publication year or data collection. Conference papers, short communications, dissertations, thesis, or technical reports also be considered due to the possibility of reducing publication bias. ... Any publication language should be considered, but the string keywords will be searched in English.",
      "reason": "Report characteristics are specified: no year restriction, grey literature (conference papers, theses, reports) allowed, and any publication language accepted."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "63 did not investigate the relationship between energy use and some independent variable, 19 did not present quantitative data for energy use and/or independent variables",
      "reason": "Exclusion reasons distinguish studies lacking the relationship/outcome from studies lacking quantitative data, but the review does not explicitly distinguish outcome not measured from outcome measured but results not reported."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "S2 Table shows the independent variables retrieved from the studies included in the meta-analysis and their classification in the organizational aspect of the hotels (environmental, social, economic, or building characteristics).",
      "reason": "Synthesis groups are specified: bivariate correlations between independent variables (classified into building, economic, social, environmental dimensions) and energy use, with subgroup/meta-regression groupings (e.g., data type, hotel category, climate zone) linked to the review objective of identifying contributors to hotel energy use."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "Conference papers, short communications, dissertations, thesis, or technical reports also be considered due to the possibility of reducing publication bias.",
      "reason": "Rationales are given for notable decisions, e.g., including grey literature to reduce publication bias and retaining the more representative study when samples overlap."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 88
}

